Article 5 (Information to Be Attached)
(1) When applying for cancellation of registration concerning former land and preservation of ownership registration concerning newly developed land, the following information shall be provided to the registry office as attached information:
1. Information from closed land registers concerning the former land;
2. Information from land registers concerning the newly developed land;
3. Detailed statements by lot number concerning the former and finally confirmed land;
4. Information substantiating the public notice of final implementation of the cadastral registers.
(2) When applying for a registration falling under Article 2 (2) 1, the matters set forth in the subparagraphs of Article 81 (1) of the Registration of Real Estate Act shall be provided to the registry office as attached information.
(3) When applying for a registration falling under any subparagraph of Article 2 (2), information substantiating the cause of registration need not be provided.
(4) In cases under Article 4 (5), a cadastral map indicating the portion over which the relevant right continues shall be provided to the registry office as attached information.
